# Codegen gains: base against candidate (#6414)

Base: `<case>/fake-jet`. Candidate: `<case>/fake-jet`.
Wall time is the best of 1 runs, taken in rounds of every variant back to back (odd rounds in reverse order) on CPU 0. Control is the base binary measured again as its own variant: its change against base is the noise floor, and a candidate change inside it is not a gain. RSS is the largest peak (ru_maxrss) of those runs; Linux counts it in per-CPU batches, so a peak under a few hundred KiB can read 0. Bytes are the stripped size (file bytes the PT_LOAD segments map). Ceiling is the hand-written assembly reference (asm-parity cells only). Change is candidate against base; negative is better.

